   "id": "yevamot.107b.12",
   "daf": "107b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "בֵּית שַׁמַּאי אוֹמְרִים: תְּמָאֵן וְכוּ׳. וְהָא מֵיאֲנָה חֲדָא זִימְנָא! אָמַר שְׁמוּאֵל: עַד שֶׁתַּגְדִּיל וְתֹאמַר: ״רוֹצָה אֲנִי בַּמֵּיאוּנִים הָרִאשׁוֹנִים״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that «Beit Shammai say: She refuses» once. «And» then «she must wait until she reaches majority, and refuse, and marry.» The Gemara asks: «Didn’t she» already «refuse once?» Why must she refuse again? «Shmuel said:» Beit Shammai’s statement means: The refusal does not take effect «until she reaches majority and says: I wish» to uphold «my initial refusal,» in case she changed her mind in the interim."
  }
 ],
